<div class="page-narrow">
  <p class="page-eyebrow">Help</p>
  <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">Everything you need to know about using Desks Near Me. Can’t find your answer? <a href="/support">Get in touch</a>.</p>

  <section class="faq-group">
    <h2>Getting started</h2>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>What is Desks Near Me?</summary>
      <p>Desks Near Me is a simple, convenient way for mobile workers to find great workspace anytime, anywhere. We connect people with flexible, unused workspace — productive space for guests, profitable space for hosts.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How do I sign up?</summary>
      <p>Signing up is free. Click “Sign up” in the top corner of any page and choose whether you’re here to find a space or list one, then enter your name, email, and a password. We’ll email you a confirmation link — click it to activate your account, then log in.</p>
      <p>After that, finish your profile from your Account page so hosts and guests can learn a little about you.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>I forgot my password. Help!</summary>
      <p>Password resets aren’t self-serve just yet. Email us at support@desksnear.me and we’ll help you get back into your account.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How do I change my account info?</summary>
      <p>Log in and open your Account page from the “Account” link in the top navigation. There you can update your name, phone, and bio. Changing your email or password isn’t self-serve yet — email support@desksnear.me and we’ll take care of it.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Can I connect my social accounts (LinkedIn, Facebook, Twitter)?</summary>
      <p>Not yet — accounts are email-based for now. Social connections are something we may add down the road.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How do I cancel my account?</summary>
      <p>We’ll miss you if you go! To cancel your account, send us an email at support@desksnear.me and we’ll take care of it.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How can I message a host directly?</summary>
      <p>Direct messaging is coming soon. For now, open a host’s profile from any listing — the “View profile” card on the listing page — to see the other spaces they offer. In-app messaging and booking are on the way.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-group">
    <h2>Listing your space</h2>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Why should I create a listing on Desks Near Me?</summary>
      <p>Our marketplace gives professionals a place to find great offices and local businesses to call their home away from home. Unlike traditional classified ads, Desks Near Me connects rentable spaces with people looking for exactly that. List your space once, turn it on and off whenever you like, and set flexible terms — by the day, week, or month.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How do I create a listing?</summary>
      <p>If you signed up as a host, log in and open “My listings” from your Account. From there you can add a space with its location, details, and pricing by the hour, day, week, or month. (Photo uploads are coming soon — for now, listings use a placeholder image.)</p>
      <p>Signed up as a guest but want to host? Email support@desksnear.me and we’ll switch your account over.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>I want to sublet a portion of our office monthly and an individual desk daily. Is this possible?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Each listing lets you set prices for whichever durations you want — hourly, daily, weekly, monthly, or any mix — so you can offer a whole office monthly and a single desk daily.</p>
      <p>Add each space as its own listing (desk, meeting room, or office space) from “My listings,” set the price for each duration, and it’ll show up for people searching that space type. Turn an empty desk into revenue!</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How much does it cost to add a listing?</summary>
      <p>It’s free to list on Desks Near Me.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How will Desks Near Me help me cover my overhead?</summary>
      <p>Our marketplace helps you make better use of the unused areas and resources in your office. Don’t let that space go to waste every day or every month — turn it into revenue by listing it for professionals who’d love to work from your office while they’re in town on business, working on a project, or looking for a longer-term base for themselves or their team.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>We have a desk that sits empty every day, in the middle of our main office. Is it appropriate to list?</summary>
      <p>Yes! That desk is perfectly suited for the site. Create a listing and set daily, weekly, or monthly pricing. If you’d rather not have a long-term person there, just set daily or weekly rates only. That desk is a productive workstation for someone, and we’ll help them find it while you cover the overhead on that space.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>We laid off several employees and have an entire room vacant. How can Desks Near Me help?</summary>
      <p>There are several ways to make that space productive again without filling it with your own stuff or people — it shouldn’t be a drain on resources or sit as “wasted space.”</p>
      <p>Add some comfortable desks and chairs and a few basic touches so it feels welcoming, and offer it for daily, weekly, or monthly rental. It’s ideal for consultants on a team project or road warriors who need somewhere to work for a week or two. It could also be subleased on a more traditional long-term basis — a great option for a guest if it’s a furnished, turnkey space.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Are there any fees or hidden costs?</summary>
      <p>It’s completely free to join and list on desksnear.me right now. This may change in the future, but we’ll give you plenty of advance notice if it does. In-app booking and payments are coming soon; until then, every listing shows its pricing so guests know your rates up front.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How do people find my listing?</summary>
      <p>Guests search by city or their current location and can filter by space type — desk, meeting room, or office. Results show as a list today, with a map view on the way.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How do I add or delete photos on my listing?</summary>
      <p>Photo uploads are coming soon. For now, listings use a placeholder image — once uploads are live, you’ll manage photos from each listing in “My listings.”</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>How can I add multiple desks at one location?</summary>
      <p>From “My listings” in your Account, add each space as its own listing — repeat for as many desks or rooms as you have at that location.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Do I need to keep re-posting my listing?</summary>
      <p>No need to re-post. You can unpublish or re-publish a listing anytime from “My listings,” so it’s ready whenever your space frees up again.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>As a Host, can I approve Guest reservations?</summary>
      <p>Booking and reservation controls are coming soon — including the option to approve requests before they’re confirmed. We’ll share the details as that ships.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-group">
    <h2>Policies &amp; troubleshooting</h2>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>Is Desks Near Me responsible for contracts between Hosts and Guests?</summary>
      <p>As a business community, we help match Hosts and Guests. All agreements are between users.</p>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>I’m seeing a 500 error when trying to go to desksnear.me. How can I fix it?</summary>
      <p>To clear a permanent redirect, go to “chrome://settings/clearBrowserData” and clear only “cached images and files.” That should clear the redirect and let you back onto desksnear.me.</p>
    </details>
  </section>
</div>

